From: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath10k: don't request scan channel stats on WCN3990

The WLAN.HL.1.0.1.c6 firmware of the WCN3990 on SDM660 (Xiaomi Mi 8
Lite, platina) fatally asserts (err_qdi.c EX:wlan_process, RT:2072,
a fixed ~87ms after tuning to every scan channel) whenever the scan is
requested with WMI_SCAN_CHAN_STAT_EVENT. Bisected at runtime with WMI
flag knobs after eliminating board data, regdomain, channel powers,
trailing TLVs, firmware/modem builds, PS mode, band crossing and
regulators/clocks: clearing this single bit turns every scan from a
guaranteed firmware crash into a reliable full scan of both bands
(30 BSS found in testing). Reading the MAC cycle counters for the
channel stats appears to hit a dead hardware block on this platform.

Don't set the flag on WCN3990. Only channel survey data is lost.

Signed-off-by: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi.c
@@ -7096,7 +7096,18 @@
 		| WMI_SCAN_EVENT_FOREIGN_CHANNEL
 		| WMI_SCAN_EVENT_FOREIGN_CHANNEL_EXIT
 		| WMI_SCAN_EVENT_DEQUEUED;
-	arg->scan_ctrl_flags |= WMI_SCAN_CHAN_STAT_EVENT;
+	/* On the WCN3990 of the SDM660 (WLAN.HL.1.0.1.c6 firmware running
+	 * inside the modem, Xiaomi Mi 8 Lite) requesting channel stats makes
+	 * the WLAN firmware fatally assert (err_qdi.c EX:wlan_process,
+	 * RT:2072) a fixed ~87ms after tuning to every scan channel - active
+	 * or passive, any band, any board data. Reading the MAC cycle
+	 * counters for the stats appears to hit a dead hardware block on
+	 * this platform (rx_clear_count was already known to read frozen).
+	 * Bisected at runtime via WMI flag knobs: clearing this single flag
+	 * makes scans complete reliably. Only channel survey data is lost.
+	 */
+	if (!QCA_REV_WCN3990(ar))
+		arg->scan_ctrl_flags |= WMI_SCAN_CHAN_STAT_EVENT;
 	arg->n_bssids = 1;
 	arg->bssids[0].bssid = "\xFF\xFF\xFF\xFF\xFF\xFF";
 }
